# Stability

This page says what a release of {{ project_name }} can change.

Releases are tagged `vX.Y.Z`. Before 1.0, the version numbers mean this:

- A minor release, such as `0.2.0` to `0.3.0`, can add features and break things. It can change
{%- if kind == 'binary' %}
  an option, a setting, or what the program shows or writes.
{%- elif kind == 'service' %}
  the configuration the service reads or the interface it serves.
{%- else %}
  or remove a public item.
{%- endif %}
- A patch release, such as `0.2.0` to `0.2.1`, holds fixes and internal changes, such as
  dependency updates. It adds nothing and breaks nothing.

From 1.0, only a major release can break things.
{%- if kind == 'library' and publish_crate %}

The minimum Rust version, `rust-version` in `Cargo.toml`, is the stable Rust that the release is
built and tested with. A newer one comes only in a minor release, never in a patch release.
{%- endif %}

Each release's notes, in [CHANGELOG.md](../CHANGELOG.md) and on the GitHub release, say what
changed and what you must do before you upgrade. Read them before every minor upgrade.
{%- if kind == 'service' %}

The minor image tag, such as `0.3`, follows that minor version's patch releases only, so pulling it
never moves you to the next minor release. [Install](install.md) lists every tag.
{%- endif %}
{%- if kind != 'library' %}

## Names that stay the same

Your scripts, links and the commands in [Install](install.md) and
[Verify a release](verifying-releases.md) depend on these names, so no release changes them:

- The `vX.Y.Z` tag form.
- The release workflow, `.github/workflows/release.yml`, and the `main` branch it runs on.
- The repository, `{{ github_owner }}/{{ project_name }}`.
{%- if kind == 'binary' %}
- The {{ 'file' if release.files else 'archive' }} names [Install](install.md) lists, and the {{ '`' ~ release.checksums | default('SHA256SUMS') ~ '`' }}{{ ' and `attestation.json` files' if visibility == 'public' else ' file' }}.
{%- if visibility == 'public' %}
- What `attestation.json` holds: one Sigstore bundle, whose statement names each
  {{ 'file' if release.files else 'archive' }} [Install](install.md) lists by its name and SHA-256, so a program that updates itself
  can check a download with it.
{%- endif %}
{%- if release.installer %}
- The Windows installer's AppId, by which an install of a newer version finds and replaces the
  installed one.
{%- endif %}
{%- else %}
- The image, `ghcr.io/{{ github_owner | lower }}/{{ project_name }}`.
{%- endif %}
{%- endif %}
